{"description":"The authors' 2-DG energy stress on the wild-type model: 1000 s at basal metabolism, then calcium to 0.25 uM and glycolysis cut 100-fold for 1800 s. This is the protocol Supplemental Table 13's sensitivity analysis is computed over, and that table reproduces 72/72 here.","id":"ampk_2dg_wt","protocol":{"Ca_at_stress_uM":0.25,"condition":"WT","kGly_basal_per_s":0.5,"kGly_stress_per_s":0.005,"parameters":"nominal_params, unmodified except the knockout above","protocol":"authors' 2-DG energy stress (GSA_sampling.py)","t_basal_s":1000.0,"t_stress_s":1800.0},"provenance":{"archive_version":"github:natejlinden/AMPK@71513c063dee2e985c024099f44586be403dfc7d (branch rev1, the branch the published figures were produced on; `main` stops before the code behind Figs 6-9).","confidence":"educational_approximation","evidence_type":"Derived","fitted_to":"AMPK biosensor recordings, not exercise and not muscle fibres. The authors estimated the kinetic parameters against cytosolic AMPK activity measured with ExRai-AMPKAR (Schmitt et al., Nat Commun 13:3856, 2022), under a 2-deoxyglucose stimulus they model by cutting glycolytic ATP production 100-fold, 0.5 to 0.005 per s. Applying the fitted model to exercise is the authors' own extension, driven by Francis et al.'s calcium and ATP hydrolysis. The cell type behind those recordings is not stated in the preprint and is not guessed here. Which human muscle this run is shown under is OURS: a navigation choice, not a claim about that muscle. The authors' own reference list includes McConell et al., 'Skeletal Muscle AMPK Is Not Activated during 2 h of Moderate Intensity Exercise at ~65% in Endurance Trained Men'.","inputs":{"Ca_at_stress_uM":0.25,"condition":"WT","kGly_basal_per_s":0.5,"kGly_stress_per_s":0.005,"parameters":"nominal_params, unmodified except the knockout above","protocol":"authors' 2-DG energy stress (GSA_sampling.py)","t_basal_s":1000.0,"t_stress_s":1800.0},"integrator":"SciPy solve_ivp(method='LSODA') at the authors' rtol=atol=1e-6 \u2014 NOT diffrax Kvaerno5 with a PID controller, which needs jax and is not installed here. Checked: tightening to rtol=1e-8/atol=1e-10 moves ATP at the end of the coupled bout by 2e-6 relative and the sensor ratio by 1e-8.","known_discrepancy":"Table 13's last four rows are mislabelled upstream \u2014 the sampling script and the analysis script carry different free-parameter orders and SALib indexes by column. Reported in validation/REPORT.md, paper 2 \u00a73; it changes which parameter is called quiet, not any trajectory here.","model_id":"linden_santangeli_mm_nonessential_all","model_version":"Model 6, MM_nonessential_all \u2014 the full non-essential-activation model. RHS executed from the authors' own bytes (sha256 384aadba41e2bb7e\u2026), nominal_params and init_conds loaded from MM_nonessential_all.json unmodified.","paper_id":"doi:10.1038/s41540-025-00588-w","port_source_sha256":"e52d424aabcd54ff21d6a55987b3acde17ef51f1f2f72f0a81b7820d1c609207","scenario":"ampk_2dg_wt","series_defined_by_us":{"CaMKK_active_fraction":"OURS. CaMKK_act / (CaMKK + CaMKK_act). The authors plot CaMKK_act itself (exercise.ipynb cell 19) on an axis labelled mM; the same notebook labels the pAMPK activity axis mM/s in one cell and uM/s in the next, so their own labels do not agree and we do not adopt either.","pAMPK_fraction":"OURS. Sum of the authors' AMPK_IDX phosphorylated members (pAMPK, AMP_pAMPK, ADP_pAMPK, ATP_pAMPK) over the whole conserved AMPK pool. The pool and its conservation are the authors'; expressing it as a fraction is ours, and it is done because the archive states no concentration unit for the protein species."},"time_unit":"seconds","uncertainty":"NONE SHIPS. The authors' exercise figure is a 50-sample posterior ensemble drawn from results/param_est/.../Pathfinder.nc, which is absent from every branch of the pinned clone. One nominal-parameter trajectory ships instead. Do not read the single line as a posterior mean and do not draw a band around it.","validation":"Supplemental Table 13, the Sobol analysis computed over exactly the 2-DG protocol this scenario runs, reproduces 72/72 cells exact at 3 decimal places (max |delta| 4.8e-4). The TRAJECTORY itself has no published counterpart to be checked against: the paper publishes sensitivity indices over it, not the curve.","whose_protocol":"the authors' (GSA_sampling.py, slurm_scripts)"},"sampling":{"head_samples":0,"note":"the first `head_samples` archived samples, then every `stride`th, rounded. No interpolation or smoothing, and the resulting grid is NOT uniform \u2014 search `t`.","round_digits":6,"source":"scenarios/data_ampk/ampk_2dg_wt.json","stride":4},"series":{"ADP":[1.26749,2.75502,3.31501,3.52032,3.60587,3.6454,3.66505,3.67531,3.68086,3.68394,3.6857,3.68674,3.68738,3.6878,3.68809,3.68831,3.68848,3.68862,3.68874,3.68884,3.68894,3.68902,3.6891,3.68917,3.68924,3.6893,3.68935,3.6894,3.68945,3.6895,3.68954,3.68957,3.68961,3.68964,3.68967,3.68969,3.68972,3.68974,3.68976,3.68978,3.6898,3.68981,3.68983,3.68984,3.68986,3.68987,3.68988,3.68989,3.6899,3.68991,3.68992,3.68993,3.68993,3.68994,3.68995,3.68995,3.68996,3.68996,3.68997,3.68997,3.68997,3.68998,3.68998,3.68999,3.68999,3.68999,3.68999,3.69,3.69,3.69,3.69,3.69001,3.69001,3.69001,3.69001,3.69001,3.69001,3.69002,3.69002,3.69002,3.69002,3.69002,3.69002,3.69002,3.69002,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69003,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69004,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69005,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006,3.69006